# L §5.10 Kind and unit (round 7c): "unit(x) is x's unit as a key of the unit kind that holds it (`currencies` for a
# currency, §5.7), so `unit(x) == PLN` compares two keys; a place of unit `any` has no one unit, and unit(x) of it
# is refused (§8.4)".  q1: konto holds PLN: true; q2: false against EUR; q3: unit(p) for p in accounts on a day is a
# key of currencies.  q4 (L5_10_unit_any): a place of unit any is refused at load where the types show it.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place eurkonto: accounts EUR lives 2020-01-01..

ask q1: unit(konto) == PLN
ask q2: unit(konto) == EUR
ask q3: count(p in accounts on 2026-06-30 where unit(p) == EUR)
=== expect
q1: true
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: false
  cut 2026-12-31
q3: 1
  cut 2026-12-31
